        <workflow:Stage name="Create Poem" status="Succeeded">
          <startedAt>2026-09-03T05:05:25</startedAt>
          <baseCommit>80183def647a2d1d0336890dc6dcff7f8237d86c</baseCommit>
          <output>Execute Stage 1 modified exactly one file, blocks/org/blockml/bml/workspace/playground/NextPoem222.bml. The previous Spanish poem was replaced by a new German poem, and the surrounding metadata was kept consistent: the &lt;is> line now reads 'written in German', and the &lt;title> property was updated to 'Birke und Fliegenpilz'. Author (John Doe) and year (2026) are unchanged. Structure is preserved: a core:Documentation block whose &lt;documentation> holds four AABB-rhymed quatrains. No _meta/transform/ ModelTransformation files were touched by Execute; the change is scoped to the single playground poem block. ResultProducer.produce asks for a summary of the poem created in this stage; 'result' carries that summary as Text.</output>
          <completedAt>2026-09-03T05:07:13</completedAt>
          <task>
            <workflow:InstructionTask instructions="Create or update the block org.blockml.bml.workspace.playground.NextPoem222.bml that contains a random poem in german about a tree and a mushroom. For each execution create a new poem." />
          </task>
          <changedFiles>
            <type:FilePathEntity value="blocks/org/blockml/bml/workspace/playground/NextPoem222.bml" />
          </changedFiles>
        </workflow:Stage>
        <workflow:Stage name="Translate Poem" status="Succeeded">
          <startedAt>2026-09-03T05:07:13</startedAt>
          <baseCommit>21ed2a4aabd93aaa5198e9574f722e197affa899</baseCommit>
          <output>Execute Stage 2 (&quot;Translate Poem&quot;) modified exactly one file: blocks/org/blockml/bml/workspace/playground/NextPoem222.bml. The task was to translate the poem to Spanish, and that is what happened. The four German quatrains from Stage 1 ('Birke und Fliegenpilz') were replaced with a faithful Spanish rendering of the same content: the birch on the wooded slope with its gleaming white trunk (stanza 1), the white-spotted red fly agaric among the moss at its feet (stanza 2), the tree reassuring the mushroom against the storm and offering shelter (stanza 3), and the mushroom glowing through the night while the birch keeps watch as two unequal but close friends rooted in one spot (stanza 4). Supporting metadata was kept consistent: &lt;is> now reads 'written in Spanish', and &lt;title> was updated to 'Abedul y matamoscas'. Author (John Doe) and year (2026) are unchanged. Structure is preserved: a core:Documentation block whose &lt;documentation> holds four rhymed quatrains. The Spanish version uses AABB couplet rhyme, matching the original scheme. No _meta/transform/ ModelTransformation files were touched by Execute; the change is correctly scoped to the single playground poem block. This Stage has no ResultProducer, so no result summary is produced.</output>
          <completedAt>2026-09-03T05:08:23</completedAt>
          <task>
            <workflow:InstructionTask instructions="Translate the poem in org.blockml.bml.workspace.playground.NextPoem222.bml to spanish." />
          </task>
          <changedFiles>
            <type:FilePathEntity value="blocks/org/blockml/bml/workspace/playground/NextPoem222.bml" />
          </changedFiles>
        </workflow:Stage>
